2026-11-21: version 0.4.0

Incompatible changes
 - Return values and out parameters annotated (skip) are no longer
   returned.  This changes the results of every such function; in
   GLib, for example, uri:split no longer returns a leading #t.  A
   function whose only result is a skipped boolean is no longer named
   as a predicate (no "?").
 - flags-difference is now set difference; it used to return the
   symmetric difference.
 - flags->list no longer lists zero-valued flags, such as 'none,
   unless no flag is set.
 - libguile-gi now exports only its module initialization functions
   (libtool interface 7:0:0).

New features
 - New (gi girepository) module: a binding of libgirepository for
   inspecting typelibs.
 - Builds with Guile 3.0 and current GLib and GObject Introspection
   releases (tested with GLib 2.72 and 2.80), and on MinGW/UCRT.
 - Generated documentation shows optional arguments after #:optional,
   lists only the values a procedure actually returns, documents boxed
   types, and parses gi-docgen Markdown (headings of any level, fenced
   code).  A new test checks that documented signatures match the
   generated procedures.
 - Fundamental instance types that libraries introduce, such as Gtk4's
   GtkExpression, can be passed to and returned from functions and
   stored in properties and <GValue>s.
 - Deprecated entries of a typelib, such as GTK 4's tree widgets, can
   be loaded in bulk: use-typelibs takes #:deprecated? #t after a
   typelib, typelib->module takes #:deprecated?, and infos takes an
   optional argument.  They are still left out by default.  The
   documentation generators match: typelib in (gi documentation) takes
   #:deprecated?, and gi-gtkdoc takes --deprecated.
 - Field accessors.  The public fields of structs, unions and objects
   have getters such as rgba:red, and fields of plain data that the
   typelib marks writable also have setters, rgba:set-red! or set! on
   the getter.  The generated documentation lists them.
 - Virtual functions.  register-type takes #:vfuncs, a list of
   (NAME . PROCEDURE) overriding virtual functions of the parent type,
   its ancestors or its interfaces, and #:interfaces, a list of
   interfaces for the new type to implement, so that Scheme can define
   GTK widgets that draw and size themselves, or implement GListModel.
   Each virtual function also has a procedure that calls a given
   class's implementation, such as widget:do-snapshot, for chaining up.
   The generated documentation lists them.
 - The plain structs without a GType that GTK, GSK and GDK need are
   bound as foreign objects, with constructors and field accessors:
   GskRoundedRect, GskColorStop, GskShadow, GskParseLocation,
   GtkCssLocation, GdkKeymapKey, GdkTimeCoord, GtkPageRange,
   GtkRequestedSize, GtkRecentData and GtkPadActionEntry, and the
   opaque GdkToplevelSize, GdkDragSurfaceSize and
   GtkBuildableParseContext.  The functions that use them, such as
   GSK's rounded clips, gradients and shadows, are now bound.

Bug fixes
 - Fix many crashes, double frees and leaks in argument marshalling:
   reading objects back out of <GValue>s, in/out GClosure values,
   transfer-none GPtrArray results, arrays of structs stored by value,
   transfer-container arrays, and elements of transfer-full lists and
   arrays.
 - User-defined GObject types now chain up dispose and finalize, and
   subclasses of user-defined types store their properties correctly.
 - Scheme callbacks now write output arguments to the right place, and
   one procedure can serve as two callback types.
 - Fix crashes and wrong results throughout (gi girepository).
 - Errors raised by a custom logger no longer escape into the code
   being logged.
 - typelib->module and typelib work without a version.
 - The main-loop test works with GLib 2.88, which moved
   unix_fd_add_full to GLibUnix (#144).
 - surface->cairo is now exported by (gi compat).
 - Builds with -DNDEBUG no longer break boxed types.
 - GObjects passed to C with transfer full, including those that
   Scheme callbacks return, get a reference of their own; C used to
   release the Scheme object's reference.
 - Scheme callbacks receive inout arguments' values instead of their
   addresses, can have arguments that are callbacks and enum or flags
   outputs, and report Scheme errors as GErrors when the callback can
   throw one.
 - Generated documentation no longer nests paragraphs for docstrings
   that start with whitespace.
 - Reading a property or <GValue> that holds a NULL or empty GValue,
   such as GtkDropTarget:value, or a NULL GString, returns #f instead
   of crashing.  A <GValue> holding a GValue can be set to #f or to
   another <GValue>.
 - equal? is true of two Scheme objects that refer to the same GObject
   (#123).
 - Scheme callbacks and virtual functions can fill in structs that
   their caller allocates and modify structs they are passed, so that
   a GtkTreeModel can be implemented in Scheme (#94), as
   examples/tree-model.scm does.  A
   caller-allocated output is now an argument for the procedure to
   fill in, not a value for it to return; returning one used to
   overwrite the caller's struct with a pointer.
 - Boxed values passed to C with transfer full, including those that
   Scheme callbacks return, such as the GtkTreePath of GtkTreeModel's
   get_path, are copied; C used to free the Scheme object's own.
 - Fields that hold an untyped pointer (gpointer), such as a
   GtkTreeIter's user_data, have setters.

Thanks to
 - Maxim Cournoyer <apteryks>
 - Bqleine

2021-12-29: version 0.3.2
 - SCM GObject arguments should better preserve their type when
   passing through function calls, and not downgrade to the argument's
   required type (#104)
 - Handle GVariant arguments
 - Handle GBoxed module variables
 - Initial handling of Gtk4's GtkExpression and other new, fundamental
   types
 - More verbose warnings
 - More stringent typechecks
 - Avoid crashes cause by calling callbacks in non-guile mode
 - Avoid Unicode combining character in test case

Thanks to
 - LordYuuma
 - Bob131
 - Danny Milosavljevic <daym>
 - Lloyd Konneker <bootchk>

2020-12-31: version 0.3.1
 - Marshall GValues containing pointers
 - Add compatibility functions for guile-cairo
 - Marshall GValues containing boxed types
 - Handle in/out GClosures (#82, #83)
 - Allow the return of multiple values from signal handlers
 - Fix errors associated with defining properties of GObject or GInterface
   classes
 - Fix crash caused by passing NULL values to GClosures (#102)
 - Improve handling of the loading of shared libraries, reducing the
   incidence of problems caused when guile-gi loads a different GLib
   or GObject version than the one a dlopened library may depend on
 - Handle some GInterface types
 - Marshall arrays of GTypes
 - Add a workaround for 'make check' failures in Guix environments

 Thanks to assistance and reporting by
 - Danny <daym>
 - Detlev Zundel <laodzu>
 - Danny O'Brien <dannyob>
 - Arun Isaac <arunisaac>


2020-03-24: version 0.3.0
- Handle mutation operations of caller-allocated function arguments (#39)
  - Some procedures with preallocated in/out arguments will now bear the
    mutation sigil `!'
- Clean up output argument processing (#39)
  - This may re-order the output arguments of some procedures
- Use conventional installation directory for binary guile extensions (#72)
- Improve Guix build and install
- Stricter errors for callbacks and signals
- Don't prematurely catch errors thrown by callbacks in the callback handler
- New custom logger
- New hook procedures for inspecting FFI calls
- Better tests for callback, signals, arrays (#54, #57)
- Clean up debug info (#77)
- Updated docs (#76)
- Bug fixes

2020-01-27: version 0.2.2
- Add Guile 3.0 to configure
- Callback fixes (#68, #70)
  - Prevent garbage collection of callbacks before use
  - Fix unpacking of integers in callbacks
  - Harmonize the calling convention of callback parameters
    with the calling convention of introspected C functions
- Some support for GHashTable types (#56)
- Improvements to autogenerated documentation (#50)
- Bug fixes

2019-11-01: version 0.2.1
- Improved efficiency in build and test
  - Non-recursive make
  - SRFI-64-based tests (#63)
  - Use system's gimarshallingtests
- Better support for GArray, GPtrArray, and GByteArray (#54)
- Improve generation of documentation for properties and enums
- Add subcategories to GLib-based logging
- More general documentation
- Bug fixes

2019-09-02: version 0.2.0
- Improvements in SCM <-> C argument conversion
  - simplified to GType + metadata (#31)
  - more type associations (#25)
    - enum and flags classes, plus an API for them (#33)
    - procedure wrappers for callbacks and closures
    - accessor wrapper for values
    - integer data types must be `<integer>`
    - float and double must be `<real>`
- Support generation of documentation
  - In-REPL documentation through guile-procedures.txt (#24)
  - Docbook XML (#23)
  - Add gtkdoc support through `gi-gtkdoc` (use `guild` to invoke)

2019-08-02: version 0.1.0
- Improvements in procedure generation
  - Use of GOOPS-based methods with short names
  - Renaming scheme applied to "namespaces" as well.
- Mapping of GObject oriented programming to GOOPS
  - added signals
  - added properties as accessors
- Improvements in C-to-SCM procedure argument conversions
  - Implicitly handle length arguments
  - Support for more types
- Better Typelib support
  - allow loading of single infos
  - prevent accidental leaking of definitions into the wrong module
- Support building with GCOV.

